  "code": "def factor_smoothed_left_tail_variance_share(df):\n    \"\"\"Exponentially smoothed share of realized variance attributable to negative returns.\"\"\"\n    df_copy = df.copy()\n    ret = df_copy[\"close\"].pct_change()\n    downside_energy = ret.clip(upper=0.0).pow(2).ewm(span=30, min_periods=20, adjust=False).mean()\n    total_energy = ret.pow(2).ewm(span=30, min_periods=20, adjust=False).mean()\n    df_copy[\"factor_smoothed_left_tail_variance_share\"] = downside_energy / total_energy.replace(0.0, np.nan)\n    return df_copy[\"factor_smoothed_left_tail_variance_share\"]",
  "cross_sectional_rationale": "The bounded downside-variance share is a relative same-day fragility measure: ranking identifies stocks with the most loss-dominated return variance among contemporaries while reducing sensitivity to market-wide changes in realized volatility.",
